<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Military settlement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1810">1810</a>–<a href="/years/1857">1857</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Military settlements</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Military settlements were an organization of the Russian army from 1810 to 1857 that combined military service with farming, introduced by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-i-of-russia">Alexander I</a> to create an inexpensive reserve of trained troops. Alexei Arakcheyev set up the first in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mogilev">Mogilev</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a> in 1810–1812 and headed all of them from 1817; by 1825 they made up almost a quarter of the army by some accounts. Life was strictly regulated, corporal punishment was common, and drill left the farm work late. Settlers rose in the Chuguyev regiment in 1819 and near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/staraya-russa">Staraya Russa</a> in July 1831, when the rebels executed their superiors; both risings were harshly put down, and all the settlements were abolished in 1857.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/military-settlement.jpg" alt="Military settlement" width="330" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: « Военная энциклопедия И. Д. Сытина ». (Санкт-Петербург; 1912). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Карта_к_статье_«Военные_поселения»._Военная_энциклопедия_Сытина_(Санкт-Петербург,_1911-1915).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
